The graph shows the value of a compressor depreciated by the straight-line method.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=9cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=6.6,ymin=0,ymax=44000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6},ytick={0,5000,10000,15000,20000,25000,30000,35000,40000},grid=both,samples=2,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years, $n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:6]{40000 - 5000*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
If the depreciation continues at the same rate, after how many years will the compressor be worth $\$0$?
